WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.040
[Numbers count down.]

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:36.200
[Music]

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:43.930
[Narrator:] ...upon which they place drops and inhale the smoke through tubes inserted in their nostrils.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:49.320
This was the first acquaintance of white men with tobacco.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:55.150
The fragrant leaves of the Indians quickly spread around the world.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:01:02.430
Today the labor and skill of thousands of families goes into the growing and processing of tobacco.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.890
Tobacco plants grow on millions of acres of fertile soil.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:10.820
Soil that might otherwise be used to produce food.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.330
From pure tobacco leaves,

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:19.320
such generally known products such as snuff, chewing tobacco, pipe tobacco, cigars, and cigarettes are made.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.910
More stores sell tobacco than bread,

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:26.710
and money spent on tobacco could pay for half our schools.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:31.800
This then is an example of a product that represents one of America's largest farm crops,

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:35.600
and one of the most controversial consumer articles.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:40.590
What does this product contain and how does it affect those who use it?

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:44.130
What tobacco smoke contains is simple to determine.

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:46.930
Here is a scientifically designed apparatus

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:51.270
for collecting the content of the smoke under controlled conditions.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:54.680
Smoking is a process of dry distillation.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:03.520
By dry distillation, we mean the transformation of dry substances into vapor.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.190
As the tobacco is smoked,

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:08.510
all the products normally inhaled by a smoker are collected

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:14.480
in these bottle traps filled with liquids.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.860
Supplementary traps called bubblers

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.180
catch any substances not collected in the flasks.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.030
The liquid in two of the flasks absorbs the nicotine,

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:31.650
and in the other two flasks it collects the tarry substances out of the burning tobacco.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:37.170
From the first group of flasks, chemists isolate nicotine by distillation.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:40.030
The amount of nicotine obtained in this process, is of course,

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:44.990
small and can only be measured by very delicate instruments.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.530
The ultra-violet spectrophotometer for instance,

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:51.600
is often used to measure minute amounts of nicotine.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.200
Different cigarettes, even of the same brand,

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:57.910
sometimes vary in weight and quantity of nicotine.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:03.960
Variations from one to three milligrams per cigarette have been recorded.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:05.400
One milligram is about this much,

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:10.640
and three times this amount could cause nicotine poisoning.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.830
The liquid in the second pair of flasks contains tars.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:21.980
It is first diluted with water, then chloroform is added.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:27.630
The chloroform dissolves the tars from the solution.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.150
Since chloroform and water do not mix,

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:32.220
the chloroform mixture separates from the water

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.610
as soon as the shaking stops.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:39.280
Finally, chloroform is evaporated out of the mixture by boiling,

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:44.000
leaving the tars behind in the measuring cup.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:46.780
Cigarette tars consist of a variety of substances,

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.350
which can be further separated chemically.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:56.470
Here are some of the more important constituents of cigarette tars.

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:59.560
Some may be considered irritants, others, stimulants,

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:03.820
and some as having no known effect upon the human organism.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.990
All smoke, including cigarette smoke,

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.450
contains some carbon monoxide,

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:12.800
a poisonous gas that combines readily with the hemoglobin of the red blood cells,

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:18.550
and prevents it from absorbing oxygen in the lungs and giving it off to the tissues.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:25.800
Very little is known about how much harm carbon monoxide from smoking does.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:29.360
All these tarry substances are the products of burning.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:32.900
They are not in the green tobacco leaves.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:37.640
But unlike tars, nicotine is found in the unburned tobacco.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:41.540
In smoking, some of the nicotine enters the body.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.890
When we light a cigarette,

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:47.730
about 25 percent of the nicotine is destroyed chemically by fire.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:52.560
Behind the glowing tip, in the zone where tobacco is heated to a medium temperature,

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:57.170
gases containing nicotine arise from the leaves.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:00.780
About 30 percent of these gases pass out into the atmosphere,

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.540
while the remaining 45 percent continue to flow

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:07.360
with the main air current towards the mouth.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:10.890
However, the major portion of the nicotine does not reach the mouth.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:16.560
It is deposited on the cold tobacco particles which it passes on the way.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:24.270
In consequence, only some fifteen percent of the total quantity of nicotine enters the mouth.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:29.390
Nicotine enters the body primarily through the air-passages and lungs.

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:33.790
However, some nicotine is dissolved in the saliva of the mouth and swallowed,

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:39.220
thus reaching the stomach directly.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:42.580
From the stomach, the portal vein carries it to the liver,

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:47.660
where some chemical changes occur which are not yet fully understood.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.660
But most of the nicotine enters the lungs with the inhaled air.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.890
From the lungs, it is carried to the left side of the heart,

00:05:55.910 --> 00:06:00.520
and from there it is rapidly distributed to all tissues of the body.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:07.420
This is why the smoker feels the effects of smoking almost as soon as he lights the tobacco.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:11.270
Carried by the blood, nicotine reaches the nerve cells,

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:15.630
where it induces a complex set of reactions.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:19.230
The drug acts mainly on three parts of the nervous system:

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:23.570
on the ganglia, or switchboards, of the autonomic nervous system,

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:29.870
on the junction between nerves and the muscle, and on the brain itself.

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:34.110
At these points, nicotine first stimulates the nerve cells,

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:38.640
then gradually slows down functions and even paralyzes them.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.670
As a consequence, many types of reactions may go on at different rates

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:45.930
and at different places in the body simultaneously,

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:49.360
producing involved and often unpredictable effects,

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:54.040
effects which vary with each individual.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:59.960
Animal experiments enable us to observe the action of massive doses of nicotine.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:03.070
Note the blood vessels in this rabbit's ear.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:11.260
An injection of nicotine affects the rabbit's blood vessels dramatically.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:15.790
Watch how the small arteries in the rabbit's ear gradually disappear

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:17.810
as the blood vessels tighten up

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:37.660
under the stimulating action of nicotine.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.240
In this experimental setup,

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:45.710
effects of nicotine from smoking can be measured with special instruments.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:49.110
Although the smoker absorbs relatively small amounts of nicotine,

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.980
sensitive instruments can record its effect.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:58.010
For instance, these thermal couples record the influence of nicotine upon the body temperature.

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:02.050
In this experiment, we see that the skin temperature gradually drops

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:03.680
from .80 on the graph

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:08.600
to about 65, or 15 points.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:11.490
The skin temperature drops because blood vessels constrict

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.150
under the influence of nicotine,

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:18.220
and less blood reaches the skin.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:21.350
Experiments with animals help dramatize the effect of nicotine

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:23.930
on the nerve cells of the heart.

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:28.020
By applying the drug directly to the exposed nerve of a rabbit's heart,

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:35.460
we induce a change in rhythm.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.050
To understand better what is happening,

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.640
let us look at a schematic drawing.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:44.600
In the experiment, nicotine was applied at the spot indicated by the arrow.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:49.010
And this is one nerve cell called a ganglion cell.

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:55.430
Nicotine first stimulates the nerve cells, then it paralyzes them.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:58.050
See how the rabbit's heart first beats slower,

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:01.940
then speeds up as the nicotine stimulates and subsequently

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:09.270
paralyzes the nerve cells of the heart.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:10.440
In the observation chamber,

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:14.410
the research scientist can measure simultaneously the action of nicotine

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:20.930
upon the human heart, breathing, skin temperature, and blood pressure.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:23.370
The multiple graph indicates that this man's heart

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:27.130
has not been visibly affected by the nicotine.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:31.860
The graph in the middle reproduces the pattern of breathing.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:37.970
We've seen that nicotine causes the heart to beat more rapidly and often irregularly.

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:41.830
We've also seen that nicotine causes blood vessels to contract.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.220
There is a connection between the two.

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:45.780
When the heart beats faster,

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:48.090
it pumps more blood through the blood vessels,

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:50.370
which nicotine has made narrower.

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:54.000
As a result, blood pressure increases.

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:57.500
Smoking is dangerous for persons suffering from disorders of blood vessels

00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:03.080
of the extremities, such as in the case of Berger's disease.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:07.160
To demonstrate the action of the autonomic ganglion cells of the intestines,

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:10.740
we place a piece of rabbit intestine in a glass container.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.310
The rhythmic movement of the intestine continues

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:16.270
even after it is separated from the animal.

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:20.610
The scribe shows normal peristalsis.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:27.520
Now we inject nicotine into the solution.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.320
The reaction is violent.

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:32.760
This is one reason why doctors often advise patients

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:41.130
with peptic ulcers, chronic heartburn, or spastic intestines to abstain from smoking.

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:44.240
Nicotine also acts upon the central nervous system.

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:47.800
It stimulates it and produces a quickening of brain activity

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:52.600
which creates a feeling of nervousness and excitement.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:58.510
This rabbit reacts calmly to petting and tapping.

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:00.480
But as soon as nicotine has acted upon it,

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:11.110
the rabbit reacts to the same treatment with convulsions and tremors.

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:15.930
Nicotine that enters the lungs of the smoker spreads rapidly through the body.

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:21.230
In turn it is excreted in urine, saliva, and sweat.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:24.560
After several days all nicotine leaves the body,

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:27.540
but the urge to smoke remains.

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:30.790
This urge is the result of a complex set of causes,

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:33.130
most of them psychological.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:35.390
Contrary to other habit-forming drugs,

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:40.020
no bad aftereffects are known to result from giving up smoking.

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:43.800
The question is then, why do people smoke?

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:46.140
[Woman 1:] It's sociable.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:48.180
[Man:] I never thought why I smoke.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:51.180
[Woman 2:] I started smoking when I was quite young.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:56.940
[Woman 3:] My parents smoke, so do I.

00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:00.120
[Narrator:] Most people start smoking in imitation of a hero

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.900
or because they think that it makes them look important,

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.630
grown-up, or sophisticated.

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:08.240
Or they just stumble into the habit.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:12.090
But once formed it is a hard habit to break.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:18.050
On the other hand, smoking is not an inborn, inherited, or natural urge.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:23.580
Beginners almost without exception find smoking irritating.

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:27.270
Sometimes reactions are quite violent,

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:30.680
and yet smoking is a widespread social habit,

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:36.240
so widespread that considerable money is spent on the study of its effects.

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:39.470
What are the conclusions of research at this time?

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:41.240
For one thing, there seems to be agreement

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:44.190
that smoke causes irritation of air passages.

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:46.320
[Man coughs as smoke swirls around him.]

00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:50.060
A smoker's cough is a well-known sound.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.960
Of the many tar compounds in the tobacco smoke,

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:57.840
we cannot tell with certainty which one, or ones, cause irritation.

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:01.910
Our way of life makes it necessary for many people to live in air polluted

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:05.540
with industrial smoke, dust, and car exhaust.

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:08.680
Add to this the irritation of tobacco smoke

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:12.730
and draw your own conclusions.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:16.820
Experiments with mice are being conducted in several universities.

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:19.820
Scientists suspect that certain constituents in the smoke,

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:22.350
probably some of the tarry substances,

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:25.060
may cause cancer in the respiratory tract,

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:28.940
especially in the lungs of smokers.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:33.670
By smearing tars obtained from tobacco smoke and polluted city air on the skin of mice,

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:37.790
scientists have already succeeded in inducing cancer in mice.

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:41.620
Research in this area is relatively new.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:45.350
Observers also point at the high incidence of lip and tongue cancers

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:49.510
found among pipe smokers.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:51.790
The increase in heart ailments in recent years

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.270
alerted medical research to a closer observation

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:57.340
of smoking habits of heart patients.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:58.770
There seems to be considerable agreement

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:02.220
about the effect of smoking upon the human organism.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:04.320
But a great deal more work is needed

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:11.480
to explain the potentially dangerous effects of smoke tars.

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:14.120
Smoking is a widespread social habit,

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:19.070
a habit very easily acquired but very hard to break.

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:24.030
Helped by advertising and glamourizing, it makes new converts easily,

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:27.950
especially among the young.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.090
Armed with these facts,

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:35.910
it must be the decision of each and every individual whether he or she

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:43.840
will take the risks of smoking.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:52.460
[Music]

